{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104017-redesigning-wta","id":1104017,"title":"Redesigning WtA","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-15T16:35:04-07:00","id":1104017,"title":"Redesigning WtA","content":"Since we are likely to hear about WtA5 soon, I was wondering how people who redesign WtA from first principles? What would you change in game mechanics and setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T17:38:44-07:00","id":1104051,"title":"","content":"Setting wise i wouldnt change much more than correcting the mistakes that were the CoG revised and Fianna Revised. Maaaaybe if i were to be picky about metaplot i would make Samuel Heighs a Glasswalker kin instead of a CoG kin to tie in with the whole plot point of Glasswalker kinfolks not having anything to do. Get rid of that nonsense of only kinfolk can get forge klaives.<br /> <br /> Mechanic wise though? Get rid of the damage roll. 3 rolls for combat turn. Attack, defense and soak roll. Pure-breed i would make it a trait you buy for RP or rework it as a better mechanic because right now is more broken than Generation on vampire and thats an accomplishment in ineptitude.<br /> <br /> No roll for transformation and regeneration. Learn some of the few good bit on forsaken and ditch the stupid system on WtA of rolling for things that dont need to.<br /> <br /> Garou eat aggravated from silver on all forms. Rework the gifts because as of right now they range from &quot;Must have&quot; to &quot;useless&quot; to some that are basically &quot;fuck you, i win&quot;.<br /> <br /> I am not a fan of rage mostly because multi-actions break the shitty system OWoD barely put together but i dont see how to change it as of right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 06-15-2017, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T18:03:39-07:00","id":1104063,"title":"","content":"5 tribes (alpha leaders, savage warriors, obtuse occultists, urban sophisticates, passionate revelers), 3 auspices (full, shifting, new), 2 breeds (human, wolf), and only five non-wolf shifters (jaguar, tiger, leopard, hyena and shark), the five tribes follow the five children of Father Wolf and Mother Earth, and the breeds started with the Hero Twins (one wolf-born, one human born; twin-ship is spiritual), and the auspices based on the three daughters of the moon. There are two other tribes, one of outcasts and misfits (Bonegnawers), and one of all-wolf born anti-humans (Predator Kings). There is an Ivory Priesthood devoted to Luna and a Mother Earth sect called the Children of Gaia.<br /> Primal Urge is their power stat, Rage is their energy, and Harmony is their morality system (representing the balance between man and wolf, flesh and spirit, rationality and instinct, life and death, civilization and nature). Attributes are physical/social/mental X power/finesse/resistance (Strength, Dexterity, Stamina, Charisma, Manipulation, Composure, Intelligence, Wits, Resolve) and Abilities having only 8 per type (Talents, Skills, Knowledge) and trying to keep Backgrounds to no more than ten.<br /> <br /> And I'm sure everyone would hate it. <br /> <br /> <br /> (There's also a completely different type of creature called Tricksters who have only human and animal forms, with families based on cats, ravens, hares, foxes, serpents, monkeys, and coyotes.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T18:06:07-07:00","id":1104067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104017-redesigning-wta?p=1104051#post1104051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting wise i wouldnt change much more than correcting the mistakes that were the CoG revised and Fianna Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>And those mistakes are \u2026?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T18:16:41-07:00","id":1104070,"title":"","content":"I can't speak about Revised Fianna, but CoG Revised often forgot that it was talking about werewolves. Also, the business with trying to purify a BSD with a simple rite, the rite of clouds and rain that involved breaking the first tenet of the litany to get an ostensible bonus to resist frenzy that's never described, random tangents about bondage dungeons and leathermen, BSDs bursting from porta-potties at Woodstock, Woodstock, the fucking obsession with Woodstock and hippie culture...<br /> <br /> Let's just say that the whole of the tone was far off of target.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104017-redesigning-wta?p=1104063#post1104063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 tribes (alpha leaders, savage warriors, obtuse occultists, urban sophisticates, passionate revelers), 3 auspices (full, shifting, new), 2 breeds (human, wolf), and only five non-wolf shifters (jaguar, tiger, leopard, hyena and shark), the five tribes follow the five children of Father Wolf and Mother Earth, and the breeds started with the Hero Twins (one wolf-born, one human born; twin-ship is spiritual), and the auspices based on the three daughters of the moon. There are two other tribes, one of outcasts and misfits (Bonegnawers), and one of all-wolf born anti-humans (Predator Kings). There is an Ivory Priesthood devoted to Luna and a Mother Earth sect called the Children of Gaia.<br /> Primal Urge is their power stat, Rage is their energy, and Harmony is their morality system (representing the balance between man and wolf, flesh and spirit, rationality and instinct, life and death, civilization and nature). Attributes are physical/social/mental X power/finesse/resistance (Strength, Dexterity, Stamina, Charisma, Manipulation, Composure, Intelligence, Wits, Resolve) and Abilities having only 8 per type (Talents, Skills, Knowledge) and trying to keep Backgrounds to no more than ten.<br /> <br /> And I'm sure everyone would hate it.<br /> <br /> <br /> (There's also a completely different type of creature called Tricksters who have only human and animal forms, with families based on cats, ravens, hares, foxes, serpents, monkeys, and coyotes.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You basically described first edition Forsaken with a bit of Apocalypse in it. Pretty tepid, all around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T18:17:09-07:00","id":1104071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104017-redesigning-wta?p=1104067#post1104067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And those mistakes are \u2026?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously? The problems with CoG revised are too many to account for and plenty of discussion have been made about it. Its the Gypsies book of Werewolf or the Free council book. The most glaring of them is make the entire tribe as those episode that show Lisa Simpson being self-righteous. The entire thing show the tribe as being both ineffectual and criminally negligent while preaching like a parody of middle class white guilt complex. You can read the fatal and friend review for a summary. The children of Gaia arent a group of the idea TV has of hippies who always give the other cheek because that makes them somehow superior.<br /> <br /> They are a tribe who fights for peace which is a elusive and subjective concept and whose rage is aimed at the Garou nation. They fight against the worse institution that keeps making the Garou loose them war and the issue and complexity is in how they solve it because while they fight the Garou nation they gotta live in it and move its members to change it for the better.<br /> <br /> As for the fianna, while most of the other Tribebooks in revised were pretty good. The fianna just paint them as the bro tribe. They are useless as all their roles are better fill by other tribes so all they are good at is being cannon fodder to avoid more useful garou to live and drink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 06-15-2017, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T18:23:00-07:00","id":1104078,"title":"","content":"My two favorite tribes as they stand now(as of W20) are the Fianna and the CoG. So I'd(and many others) prefer they not be changed, thank you very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T18:46:08-07:00","id":1104091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104017-redesigning-wta?p=1104071#post1104071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the fianna, while most of the other Tribebooks in revised were pretty good. The fianna just paint them as the bro tribe. They are useless as all their roles are better fill by other tribes so all they are good at is being cannon fodder to avoid more useful garou to live and drink.</div> </div> </div> </div>You were clearly reading a completely different revised Fianna Tribebook than I was. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T19:08:39-07:00","id":1104100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104017-redesigning-wta?p=1104070#post1104070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You basically described first edition Forsaken with a bit of Apocalypse in it. Pretty tepid, all around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, It was something I pulled out of my ass on the fly within three seconds of seeing the thread. Most of my better ideas are in one of the earlier threads.<br /> <br /> The only thing I was at all serious about was that I actually prefer the nWoD/CoD's attribute set up, and I really do only use 8 of each ability type in my games because it prevents skill creep and ensures the PCs remain highly competent without having to spend a large number of character points. I've also found that using power stats for each type (Blood Potency, Primal Urge, Gnosis, Memoriam, Legend, Ka) helps make crossover issues a lot easier while making it easier for PCs to ascend to heights of power, while morality systems (Humanity, Harmony, Wisdom, Psyche, Clarity, Ma'at) offer a number of interesting role-playing possibilities and can help reign in some problem players. <br /> <br /> (The Tricksters thing was something I experimented with several years ago as a replacement for most of the Fera and the Pooka, but I decided I liked the Pooka too much.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T19:19:31-07:00","id":1104112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104017-redesigning-wta?p=1104091#post1104091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You were clearly reading a completely different revised Fianna Tribebook than I was.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Let me be clear while i mentioned the CoG revised and The fianna one as the same problem to be fixed they arent on the same level of awfulness. CoG is gypsies supplement level bad while Fianna is just a mediocre book. It basically boiled down to, they like to drink, party and they make metis and every single thing they do another tribe do better.<br /> <br /> Their tribebook define 3 roles for most fiannas: Bards (as inspiring), Druids and Warriors. Thing is a competent good Silver Fang or Children of Gaia is better as inspiring or uniting than a fianna. Uktena make for far better &quot;druids&quot; than them. And Fenrir/Shadowlords are better more pragmatic warriors because they truly appreciate strength no matter the source or dont buy into the Silver Fangs bullshit when they are mad. They fail in all 3 roles that supposedly define them.<br /> <br /> I kinda like them personally because they are as unredimible as the BSD, or even less, and make for perfect black hats for intra-garou politics histories because they are just so awful with no redeeming qualities. They obnoxious drunks, Ableist, homophobic and racist. Its like all the bad unredeemable qualities in 1 group. When you play Werewolf poltics as it kinda is, GoT with fur. Then politically maneuvering the fianna to die never make player or even PCs feel bad, is like making Ramsey die. Just fun for all the family.<br /> <br /> But that does bring the problem that there isnt any depth to the tribe as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T20:20:13-07:00","id":1104126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104017-redesigning-wta?p=1104112#post1104112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let me be clear while i mentioned the CoG revised and The fianna one as the same problem to be fixed they arent on the same level of awfulness. CoG is gypsies supplement level bad while Fianna is just a mediocre book. It basically boiled down to, they like to drink, party and they make metis and every single thing they do another tribe do better.<br /> <br /> Their tribebook define 3 roles for most fiannas: Bards (as inspiring), Druids and Warriors. Thing is a competent good Silver Fang or Children of Gaia is better as inspiring or uniting than a fianna. Uktena make for far better &quot;druids&quot; than them. And Fenrir/Shadowlords are better more pragmatic warriors because they truly appreciate strength no matter the source or dont buy into the Silver Fangs bullshit when they are mad. They fail in all 3 roles that supposedly define them.<br /> <br /> I kinda like them personally because they are as unredimible as the BSD, or even less, and make for perfect black hats for intra-garou politics histories because they are just so awful with no redeeming qualities. They obnoxious drunks, Ableist, homophobic and racist. Its like all the bad unredeemable qualities in 1 group. When you play Werewolf poltics as it kinda is, GoT with fur. Then politically maneuvering the fianna to die never make player or even PCs feel bad, is like making Ramsey die. Just fun for all the family.<br /> <br /> But that does bring the problem that there isnt any depth to the tribe as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to chime in that i disagree with a lot of your interpretation on the tribe. I will say this, I agree with the ableism thing, and would love to get rid of it. It makes no sense given the importance of King Noada on their tribe, and the idea that you would strip titles from a garou over a battle scar is shear stupidity. It's an aspect of the tribe I have always declared not a part if my game.<br /> <br /> On a side note. .I really like my reptile shifters and would be big in keeping both of them around...i would just like to make the Naga easier to integrate into a non-naga game (like if I wanted a mokol\u00e8/Naga game)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 06-16-2017, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T21:17:38-07:00","id":1104144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104017-redesigning-wta?p=1104078#post1104078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My two favorite tribes as they stand now(as of W20) are the Fianna and the CoG. So I'd(and many others) prefer they not be changed, thank you very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree. I like the CoG and the Fianna as they are in W20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T22:16:29-07:00","id":1104159,"title":"","content":"For me, freaking rewrite the Red Talons so they aren't the frothy monsters to other players.<br /> <br /> In general, though, I'd say maybe push down the Apocalypse angle a bit. There is a lot of good potential in the tribes that needs exploring more. Seriously, Silver Fangs written as the houses of Game of Thrones alone would so easily explain the relationship between them and the rest of tribes.<br /> <br /> Fianna ableism and metis abuse in a tribe with a focus to family, all due to misunderstanding ONE story. At CeltSPZ stated, it makes no sense. Myths are important, but the great work done with White Howlers and the actual Picts in Tb:WH should be used on the Fianna,too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T09:15:50-07:00","id":1104320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104017-redesigning-wta?p=1104078#post1104078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My two favorite tribes as they stand now(as of W20) are the Fianna and the CoG. So I'd(and many others) prefer they not be changed, thank you very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant the Revised presentation of both tribes not the W20. Those ones are anemic but is a 2 page spread so what you gonna do? Their presentation of the children of gaia is fine is more or less on what i am saying they should be. The tribe that fight the inbreed, stupid, full of feuds cancer that is the Garou nation. They arent a tribe of pacifist but one that push for unity on the garou front. Which makes they hate on the Fenrir kind of stupid but is just a stereotype section and those are kinda bad always.<br /> <br /> Fianna representation on W20 is fine-ish, it does highlights how they are just the bro tribe. Whose only function is being cool partying/drinking buddies and cannon fodder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T10:48:50-07:00","id":1104361,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Form</b></u><u><b>s</b></u> <br /> <b>Homid</b>: Homid bred garou cannot be detected as a supernatural creature in homid form, nor get hurt by the effects of silver. Does not regenerate.<br /> <b>Glabro</b>: -1 difficulty on perception rolls, +2 strength +2 stamina, bite +0 aggravated with a grapple, claw +0 lethal, +2 speed, regenerate lethal with stamina check. -2 appearance, -1 manipulation<br /> <b>Crinos</b>: -2 difficulty on perception rolls, +4 strength +1 dexterity +4 stamina +1 bruized health level, claw +2 damage difficulty 6, bite +2 damage difficulty 5, a werewolf in crinos gain +2 on initiative and attack rolls against enemies with shorter weapon reach like homid garou with knives or crinos-hispo that use bite attacks. +4 speed after dexterity calculation on two legs and +6 on four. Regenerate lethal damage without stamina check. -1 difficulty on Frenzy checks. All social attributes become 0 when dealing with non Garou or Garou in other forms than Crinos.<br /> <b>Hispo</b>: -2 difficulty on perception rolls, +3 strength +2 dexterity +3 stamina, claw +1 aggravated damage difficulty 6, bite +2 damage difficulty 5, tripple homid speed after dexterity calculation. Regenerate lethal with stamina check.<br /> <b>Lupus</b>: Lupus bred garou cannot be detected as a supernatural creature in lupus form, nor get hurt by the effects of silver. -3 difficulty on perception rolls +2 dexterity +2 stamina, bite+1 difficulty 5, double homid speed after dexterity calculation. Does not regenerate.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Silver Damage</b></u><br /> All werewolves take normal damage from weapons made by silver as per the damage of the weapon in Homid and Lupus and unsoakable damage upgraded by one level (bashing becomes lethal and lethal becomes aggravated) in any other form.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T12:32:55-07:00","id":1104417,"title":"","content":"One HUGE thing would be to include Lodges like in Forsaken. One of the issues I can see with the setting, is that you really have the Garou Nation and BSDs and the only true viewpoint characters. Personally, I'd like there to be unaffilated factions like those who seek to cure their nature, those with very different ideas how the Nation should be, etc. Basically, add some alternative options between the current factions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T12:39:55-07:00","id":1104425,"title":"","content":"I am confused, why would anyone want to cure their Garou nature? Garou are fuzzy superheroes (and are arguably the only heroes in oWoD). It would like being cured of being a millionaire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T12:55:46-07:00","id":1104432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104017-redesigning-wta?p=1104425#post1104425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and are arguably the only heroes in oWoD). It would like being cured of being a millionaire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not disagreeing with you, but if the Garou are heroes, the Imbued are certainly in the conversation(save for Waywards, maybe).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T13:01:54-07:00","id":1104437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104017-redesigning-wta?p=1104425#post1104425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am confused, why would anyone want to cure their Garou nature? Garou are fuzzy superheroes (and are arguably the only heroes in oWoD). It would like being cured of being a millionaire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you are suddenly thrust into a society where you get beat up for being wrong, where you are forced to fight for a war you personally have no stake in, where you see others suffer for circumentances of their birth. Oh yeah, and you now are an anger filled monster that most likely killed people when changing the first time. Add to this any personal issues with ecoterrorists, cult brainwashing or just personal ethics.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of reasons to not want to be a garou, in short.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T13:10:12-07:00","id":1104443,"title":"","content":"I am still confused why being a Garou would be a net negative. Everyone in the world is involved in the war with the Wyrm, that is just part and parcel of oWoD, they are just ignorant of the fact and attribute the actions of the agents of the Wyrm to other factors. If you are going to be involved in the war with the Wyrm, it is better to know about the war than to be ignorant about the war, it is better to be against the Wyrm than to be for the Wyrm, and it is better to be Garou than it is to be random mortal victim X.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T13:20:50-07:00","id":1104452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104017-redesigning-wta?p=1104443#post1104443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am still confused why being a Garou would be a net negative. Everyone in the world is involved in the war with the Wyrm, that is just part and parcel of oWoD, they are just ignorant of the fact and attribute the actions of the agents of the Wyrm to other factors. If you are going to be involved in the war with the Wyrm, it is better to know about the war than to be ignorant about the war, it is better to be against the Wyrm than to be for the Wyrm, and it is better to be Garou than it is to be random mortal victim X.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be true, but do you think the characters know that? As far as they know, this is a group of monsters that just kidnapped them and are trying to condition them to fight like some cult. The critique of the Garou as religious zealots is accurate. Just because they ARE right does not remove the fact that they still do force people top their war and mouth off the Litany like an evangelist mouths off bible verses.<br /> <br /> And, again, Rage prevents you from holding connections with most humans, you are a murderer and now also a monster that can lash out at any point at anyone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T13:36:58-07:00","id":1104461,"title":"","content":"Murder denotes intention and malice towards the victim of the murder (or someone associated with the victim of the murder). Killing a human during frenzy would probably not be murder, though it is definitely homicide (probably manslaughter, negligent homicide, or accidental homicide). There are a number of acceptable forms of homicide in society (self-defense, defense of another, killing an active combatant during a conflict, etc), and I imagine that the majority of people would be willing to commit homicide in self-defense or defense of another.<br /> <br /> Rage only prevents you from connecting with Mortals whose Willpower is less than your Rage. A Ragabash with Rage 1 can maintain human relationships without any particular issue and even Garou with Rage 5 will be able to maintain friends among the 38% of humans with Willpower 5+. Garou are not monsters as they are not the typical werewolves of fiction, they are the epic heroes of the oWoD and are the thin furry line between humanity and the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T13:53:47-07:00","id":1104470,"title":"","content":"What are people's thoughts on the whole Rage scares people with lower wills? Would people keep that aspect of the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T15:22:32-07:00","id":1104499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104017-redesigning-wta?p=1104461#post1104461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Ragabash with Rage 1 can maintain human relationships without any particular issue and even Garou with Rage 5 will be able to maintain friends among the 38% of humans with Willpower 5+</div> </div> </div> </div>I have always found this very fact problematic, since even a starting ahroun has to play with wilpower 3-4 in order to be considered a frenzy threat. Ragabashes, theurges and philodoxes are completely out of the ''frenzied monster'' thing and galliards are not a big deal either.<br /> Keeping in mind that Rage and frenzy are moodwise and storywise a must have danger in the game, not absolute but something players should keep a careful eye and breathe in relief when it comes to pass without great casualties. <br /> <br /> There should be a mechanic that makes Rage an issue to all starting players, not only for the ahrouns or the galliards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T19:07:36-07:00","id":1104578,"title":"","content":"Why? It is the price of gaining more Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T01:10:47-07:00","id":1104640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104017-redesigning-wta?p=1104470#post1104470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are people's thoughts on the whole Rage scares people with lower wills? Would people keep that aspect of the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I like it. The whole concept of the garou is that they fight neither among the wolves nor humans. And even spirits are mostly kind of thinking them as the Hulk.<br /> <br /> However, there is the fact that people still want their pcs to have jobs and at times forget how creepy Rage is. Plus if Rage wouldn't be such an issue, Kinfolk's role would be lesser. So, I'd say keep it as it is, or try to make a rough baseline for all garou to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T05:17:41-07:00","id":1104697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1104017-redesigning-wta?p=1104578#post1104578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? It is the price of gaining more Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> Yes, but that may happen only way too later in a campaign for the 3 lower Rage auspicies, if the players that handle them don't use metagame thinking and abuse willpower purchasing as well (highly unlikely).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T05:33:10-07:00","id":1104703,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Another Idea</b></u><br /> Garou in the Umbra gain their Rage Gnosis and Wilpower stats instead of normal attributes, which may further be modified by the form they are in, so a Child of Gaia Homid Ragabash with Rage 1 Gnosis 1 and Willpower 4 in Homid will have Rage 5 Gnosis 1 and Willpower 5 in Crinos. In the replacing of power stats are added to Skills instead of normal attributes in order to calculate dice pools. So a lupus is a must have in your pack while in the umbra. This change does not prevent Garou from using the temporary counterparts of these traits, like Rage points for extra actions or Gnosis points for Fetish or Gift activation. Garou still have their normal health levels in the umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}